              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "egeō, egēre — \"to be in need (of), to lack\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pecūniā egeō. I am short of money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "egeō, egēre, eguī + ablative or genitive. Indigeō is a stronger form; English indigent comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of egeō is not settled; Lewis & Short give no sure account. English indigent comes from its compound indigeō."
            }
          ]
